  "slug": "app-01-niri-layout-parity-audit",
  "title": "app-01: Niri layout parity audit",
  "discussedAt": "",
  "contextReady": false,
  "contextReadyReason": "",
  "summary": "Catalogare gap di comportamento/animazione rispetto a Niri e validare column width reflow.",
  "description": "\n\n═══ THE THREE OPEN ITEMS, RESCUED FROM PLAN.md (2026-07-26) ═══\nFrom the 2026-06-17/18 compatibility re-check. The keybinding complaints were mostly fixed by the\nregistry rewrite; these three remain.\n\nLESSON RECORDED THERE, WORTH KEEPING: one claim (\"focus-up jumps workspaces\") was tested and proved\nFALSE. Verify behaviour by RUNNING it, not by reading a code path.\n\n1. CATALOGUE EVERY ANIMATION, for a future animation overhaul.\n   Write down the full set of motions niri animates and how — open, close, move, resize,\n   workspace-switch, view-scroll, overview. niri gives each its own spring/easing config and an off\n   switch. Then map each to what heca does today: heca appears to use one simple easing for\n   everything, with no spring physics, no per-motion config, and no way to turn animations off.\n   The deliverable of this task is the catalogue and gap list. The improvement itself is later work.\n\n2. CONFIRM WHETHER ADDING OR REMOVING A COLUMN ACTUALLY RESIZES THE OTHERS.\n   heca recomputes all column widths on every layout change — `update_all_column_widths()` runs on\n   every mutation in `heca-core/src/layout/scrolling.rs`. niri never resizes existing columns when\n   you open a new one. The open question is whether heca's recompute really changes existing widths\n   at runtime or just re-derives the same numbers.\n   TEST IT LIVE: resize a column, add and remove another, resize the window — does the first column\n   keep its size? If it reflows, switch to storing each column's width and recomputing only the\n   changed one.\n   ⚠️ This blocks mouse divider-resize (F006): it is unverified whether a manual resize persists or\n   gets recomputed away, and divider-drag would feel broken either way until this is settled.\n\n3. RE-AUDIT THE COMPAT ITEMS STILL MARKED \"UNVERIFIED\" in niri-compatibility-review.md:\n   prefix-mode timeout · whether modifiers are read from the event or from a cache · sending a\n   literal prefix key through to the terminal · the viewport/chrome coordinate math · the\n   single-animation model · the column-width double-caching.\n   Go through each against current code, run it where behaviour matters, and update the review's\n   status table.\n\nREFERENCE: `niri-compatibility-review.md` + `docs/niri-wiki/` — keep both, do NOT delete. The review\nitself needs updating to reflect current heca (flagged 2026-06-17).\n",
